# 1D Steady Heat Diffusion Test

Simple validation case for FVM implementation. Horizontal bar with fixed
temperatures at ends.


## Problem Setup

Bar geometry: 1m long, 0.1m wide. Left end at 400K, right end at 300K. Thermal
conductivity 50 W/m·K.

j(require 'jnl.cfd.geometry)
j(require 'jnl.cfd.fvm)

j(def bar-domain
  (domain
    (rect 0 0 1.0 0.2 "solid" 
          "left" "adiabatic" "right" "adiabatic")))

j(def bar-mesh
  (mesh-tris bar-domain "pzq30a0.001"))


## Field Initialization

Create context and initialize temperature field with linear guess.
j(def ctx (make-context bar-mesh))

j(add-uniform-field! ctx "T" 350.0)
j(add-constant-field! ctx "k" 50.0)


## Equation Assembly

Laplacian operator for diffusion plus Dirichlet boundaries.
j(def T-eq (make-equation bar-mesh))

j(-> T-eq
    zero!
    (laplacian! ctx "T" (expr-field ctx "k"))
    (bc-dirichlet! ctx "left" 400.0)
    (bc-dirichlet! ctx "right" 300.0))


## Solve

Create solver and solve equation directly into T field.
j(def solver (make-solver (count (ctx "T")) 1000 1e-6))

j(solve! T-eq solver ctx "T")


## Validation

Analytical solution is linear profile. Check center temperature.
j(def T-field (ctx "T"))
j(def T-vals (.field-values T-field))
j(def T-center (nth T-vals (/ (count T-vals) 2)))

j(println "Center temperature:" T-center)
j(println "Expected (analytical): 350.0 K")
j(println "Error:" (- T-center 350.0) "K")
